# RTCP compensation direction verification test — BC configuration
# ================================================================
# This test does NOT reuse the RTCP formula for expected values.
# Instead, it independently verifies:
#   1. Each stepper's physical positive direction (isolated axis moves)
#   2. RTCP compensation direction (whether X/Y move opposite to the tool tilt)
#
# Physical convention for this machine:
#   B+ => tool tilts toward X+ (right), tip moves right if uncompensated
#   C+ => rotates tool tilt direction around Z (CCW looking from above)
#
# RTCP should compensate: when B+ tilts tip right, pivot must move LEFT (X-)
# to keep tip stationary. So G1 B+10 should produce NEGATIVE X steps.
#
# Step distances (rtcp.cfg):
#   X, Y: 0.0125 mm/step  (800 steps per 10mm)
#   Z:    0.0025 mm/step   (4000 steps per 10mm)
#   B, C: 0.1125 deg/step  (~89 steps per 10 deg)
#   tool_length = 80 mm

DICTIONARY linuxprocess.dict
CONFIG rtcp.cfg

# ================================================================
# Phase 0: Home and establish known position
# ================================================================
G28 X Y Z B C

# Move to safe reference: tip=(100, 100, 80), pivot=(100, 100, 160), B=0, C=0
G92 X0 Y0 Z0 B0 C0
G1 X100 Y100 Z80 F6000
G92 X100 Y100 Z80 B0 C0

# ================================================================
# Phase 1: Verify individual axis positive directions
# Each axis moved +10 units independently, verify step sign.
# ================================================================

# X+: should produce +800 X steps (10mm / 0.0125)
G1 X110 F6000
M114
G1 X100 F6000

# Y+: should produce +800 Y steps
G1 Y110 F6000
M114
G1 Y100 F6000

# Z+: should produce +4000 Z steps
G1 Z90 F6000
M114
G1 Z80 F6000

# B+: should produce ~+89 B steps (10 deg / 0.1125)
G1 B10 F6000
M114
G1 B0 F6000

# C+: should produce ~+89 C steps
G1 C10 F6000
M114
G1 C0 F6000

# ================================================================
# Phase 2: RTCP compensation direction verification
# ================================================================

# Test A: B+10 at C=0 — tool tilts toward X+, pivot must move X-
#   X_p = 100 - 80*sin(10)*cos(0) = 100 - 13.89 = 86.11
#   X stepper should move NEGATIVE (86.11 - 100 = -13.89 mm = -1111 steps)
#   Z_p = 80 + 80*cos(10) = 80 + 78.78 = 158.78
#   Z stepper should move NEGATIVE (158.78 - 160 = -1.22 mm = -488 steps)
G1 B10 F6000
M114
G1 B0 F6000

# Test B: B+10 C+90 — tool tilts toward Y+, pivot must move Y-
# At C=90, the tilt direction rotates from X+ to Y+
#   Y_p = 100 - 80*sin(10)*sin(90) = 100 - 13.89 = 86.11
#   Y stepper should move NEGATIVE
#   X_p = 100 - 80*sin(10)*cos(90) = 100 — X stays
G1 B10 C90 F6000
M114
G1 B0 C0 F6000

# Test C: Pure tip move X+10 with no rotation — baseline
# X stepper should move POSITIVE (+800 steps)
G1 X110 F6000
M114
G1 X100 F6000

# Test D: Combined: tip moves X+10 AND B tilts 10°
# Without RTCP sign fix: X would move WRONG direction
# Tip X goes 100→110 (+10), B goes 0→10
#   X_p = 110 - 80*sin(10)*cos(0) = 110 - 13.89 = 96.11
#   from pivot=100: net X = 96.11 - 100 = -3.89 mm = -311 steps
#   Net X is NEGATIVE because pivot compensation (-13.89) exceeds tip move (+10)
G1 X110 B10 F6000
M114
G1 X100 B0 F6000

GET_POSITION
